245
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:02,800
But of course, it's
possible to have one without

246
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:07,380
the other. So if you
have a patient that has

247
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:10,960
bacteremia but doesn't have
any evidence of a valvular

248
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:14,360
vegetation, then it's
pretty broad where that

249
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:17,620
infection can be coming
from, right? So you can

250
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:20,300
consider a whole host of
different possibilities.

251
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:23,100
Certainly in a non
-exhaustive list, you know,

252
00:15:23,100 --> 00:15:25,480
you can consider an
intravascular catheter,

253
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,600
a prosthetic joint.
There's a whole bunch

254
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,860
of reasons why you
might have an infection.

255
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:35,160
in terms of having a
valvular vegetation but no

256
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:37,800
bacteremia well then you
might be in a situation where

257
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:41,050
you have a true case of
non-bacterial thrombotic

258
00:15:41,050 --> 00:15:44,600
endocarditis or perhaps you
have a different type of

259
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:48,520
