470
00:29:13,050 --> 00:29:20,430
So generally speaking, if
myocarditis is presumed

471
00:29:20,430 --> 00:29:23,150
to be the issue, the
treatments and interventions

472
00:29:23,150 --> 00:29:26,350
are really going to be
individualized for the

473
00:29:26,350 --> 00:29:30,450
particular patient based on
their own clinical context.

474
00:29:34,010 --> 00:29:37,270
All right, so we're going
to move on here, moving

475
00:29:37,270 --> 00:29:40,390
from the inside of the heart
to the outside of the heart.

476
00:29:40,390 --> 00:29:43,670
We're going to take a
look at pericarditis, and

477
00:29:43,670 --> 00:29:47,730
pericarditis is basically
just a generalized term for

478
00:29:47,730 --> 00:29:51,390
inflammation associated
with the pericardium, and

479
00:29:51,390 --> 00:29:54,930
that is the sac around your
heart. Now, that structure

480
00:29:54,930 --> 00:29:58,410
has two basic layers to
it. So there's an external

481
00:29:58,410 --> 00:30:02,230
fibrous layer, the fibrous
pericardium, and then there's

482
00:30:02,230 --> 00:30:06,530
an internal serous
pericardial layer, which is

483
00:30:06,530 --> 00:30:11,270
itself two membranes. It's
a double membrane layer that

484
00:30:11,270 --> 00:30:14,630
has a cavity in the middle
that holds somewhere in

485
00:30:14,630 --> 00:30:17,590
the order of approximately
50 milliliters of fluid.

486
00:30:18,230 --> 00:30:21,490
Now, the pericardium
also is going to have

487
00:30:21,490 --> 00:30:23,550
some functionality
to it, right? So it's

488
00:30:23,550 --> 00:30:26,230
going to help with
cardiac efficiency.

489
00:30:26,390 --> 00:30:29,690
It'll help distribute
pressure and

490
00:30:29,690 --> 00:30:31,670
hydrostatic forces
around the heart.

491
00:30:32,130 --> 00:30:36,370
It obviously creates a
closed chamber, and that

492
00:30:36,370 --> 00:30:39,870
chamber is going to have
pressure that is different

493
00:30:39,870 --> 00:30:42,350
than atmospheric pressure,
which is going to help

494
00:30:42,350 --> 00:30:45,830
with chamber fillings,
specifically the atria.

495
00:30:46,850 --> 00:30:49,230
It's a structure
that protects the

496
00:30:49,230 --> 00:30:51,350
heart from any
type of friction.

497
00:30:52,010 --> 00:30:55,300
It's a barrier against
infection. infection

498
00:30:55,300 --> 00:30:58,320
and then obviously it
also has some anatomical

499
00:30:58,320 --> 00:31:00,950
function to it where
it helps to place

500
00:31:00,950 --> 00:31:03,290
and fix the heart
within the chest cavity.

501
00:31:06,790 --> 00:31:10,730
All right so typically
cases of pericarditis

502
00:31:10,730 --> 00:31:14,770
are going to be idiopathic
and while sometimes

503
00:31:14,770 --> 00:31:17,890
the exact cause is not
going to be known oftentimes

504
00:31:17,890 --> 00:31:20,710
it's going to be
presumed that the case is

505
00:31:20,710 --> 00:31:22,470
going to be tied to some
sort of immune system

506
00:31:22,470 --> 00:31:26,310
dysfunction or some
sort of viral infection.

507
00:31:26,530 --> 00:31:31,010
In the case of viral
pericarditis, the infection

508
00:31:31,010 --> 00:31:33,470
is typically going to
be self-limiting and is

509
00:31:33,470 --> 00:31:36,250
rarely going to be fatal.
Now if we take a look

510
00:31:36,250 --> 00:31:40,370
at some of the viral
causes, they certainly

511
00:31:40,370 --> 00:31:44,370
mirror those that we saw
in myocarditis as well

512
00:31:44,370 --> 00:31:48,910
with NR viruses like
Coxsackie viruses being the

513
00:31:48,910 --> 00:31:52,050
most common typical
agent that you would see.

514
00:31:52,270 --> 00:31:55,130
But then other common
viruses as well,

515
00:31:55,130 --> 00:31:57,810
like adenoviruses
or the flu, COVID,

516
00:31:58,070 --> 00:32:02,130
different varieties of
herpes viruses, among others.

517
00:32:03,070 --> 00:32:07,490
All right, now, while
viral infections are

518
00:32:07,490 --> 00:32:11,010
the overall leading
cause of pericarditis,

519
00:32:11,420 --> 00:32:13,920
you can also have a
bacterial infection.

520
00:32:14,670 --> 00:32:18,230
That might be a little
less common, but it has

521
00:32:18,230 --> 00:32:21,570
potential to be a little
bit more dangerous. In that

522
00:32:21,570 --> 00:32:27,630
case, the typical common
causative agents in

523
00:32:27,630 --> 00:32:30,870
areas of the world like
North America and Europe

524
00:32:30,870 --> 00:32:34,470
are going to be strep
pneumoniae and staph aureus.

525
00:32:34,690 --> 00:32:37,850
Now, if you have these
bacterial species

526
00:32:37,850 --> 00:32:40,910
causing pericarditis,
it would then be

527
00:32:40,910 --> 00:32:43,610
referred to as
purulent pericarditis.

528
00:32:44,150 --> 00:32:48,310
So the way these bacteria
can access the pericardium

529
00:32:48,310 --> 00:32:51,530
could be just through
the bloodstream, could

530
00:32:51,530 --> 00:32:55,190
be direct extension
maybe from pneumonia, or

531
00:32:55,190 --> 00:33:00,050
maybe rare cases following
a surgical procedure.

532
00:33:01,010 --> 00:33:04,650
All right, now if we consider
the most common cause

533
00:33:04,650 --> 00:33:08,590
globally in that case, then
mycobacterium tuberculosis

534
00:33:08,590 --> 00:33:12,460
would be the most common
cause of pericarditis. and

535
00:33:12,460 --> 00:33:15,690
in that case, generally
speaking, it's going to produce

536
00:33:15,690 --> 00:33:20,190
a subacute chronic form of
pericarditis. Of course,

537
00:33:20,190 --> 00:33:22,710
this is going to be the
causative agent of tuberculosis

538
00:33:22,710 --> 00:33:27,670
and so this would be the
most common cause in any

539
00:33:27,670 --> 00:33:31,390
area of the world where
tuberculosis is also endemic.

540
00:33:31,930 --> 00:33:36,890
Now lastly, you could also
have fungi being the cause

541
00:33:36,890 --> 00:33:40,990
of pericarditis, although
it would be somewhat rare.

542
00:33:41,210 --> 00:33:45,070
So different types
of fungi like candida

543
00:33:45,070 --> 00:33:48,230
or aspergillus or
histoplasma could be the

544
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:50,540
microbial cause of
it if it is a fungus.

545
00:33:54,110 --> 00:33:56,990
So what are we looking for in

546
00:33:56,990 --> 00:33:59,190
a patient with pericarditis?

547
00:33:59,250 --> 00:34:03,090
So one of the main symptoms
is going to be chest pain.

548
00:34:03,090 --> 00:34:06,490
And that pain generally is
going to be worse when the

549
00:34:06,490 --> 00:34:11,070
patient is inhaling or lying
down. And so oftentimes

550
00:34:11,090 --> 00:34:14,070
individuals with pericarditis
are going to want to sit

551
00:34:14,070 --> 00:34:17,530
up or lean forward to be
able to alleviate that pain.

552
00:34:17,670 --> 00:34:21,050
You might also see generalized
symptoms like a fever

553
00:34:21,050 --> 00:34:24,710
or other just, you know,
constitutional symptoms as

554
00:34:24,710 --> 00:34:28,510
well, in addition to something
known as a friction rub.

555
00:34:28,750 --> 00:34:31,710
And a friction rub is kind of

556
00:34:31,710 --> 00:34:33,750
a hallmark of pericarditis.

557
00:34:34,070 --> 00:34:38,470
What that is, it's basically
a high-pitched, scratchy

558
00:34:38,470 --> 00:34:42,230
sound that's generated
by the inflamed layers of

559
00:34:42,230 --> 00:34:44,590
the pericardium that are
rubbing against each other.

560
00:34:45,370 --> 00:34:48,750
Now, during your workup,
you might also use other

561
00:34:48,750 --> 00:34:52,290
diagnostic tests, like
an ECG, where you might

562
00:34:52,290 --> 00:34:57,110
see changes in the PR or
the ST segments, and you

563
00:34:57,110 --> 00:35:00,030
might also use imaging
as well. So what you're

564
00:35:00,030 --> 00:35:02,650
looking for there is
some sort of pericardial

565
00:35:02,650 --> 00:35:07,110
effusion, so more fluid
entering into that pericardial

566
00:35:07,110 --> 00:35:10,510
space, and you might
be able to see that on

567
00:35:10,510 --> 00:35:16,130
an echo or a CMR imaging
or with a chest x-ray.

568
00:35:16,250 --> 00:35:18,830
And what you're looking
for is basically just

569
00:35:18,830 --> 00:35:21,190
an enlargement of the
cardiac silhouette,

570
00:35:21,770 --> 00:35:25,510
like you can see on
the image on the slide.

571
00:35:28,550 --> 00:35:30,450
All right, so
let's consider some

572
00:35:30,450 --> 00:35:32,890
complications to pericarditis.

573
00:35:33,070 --> 00:35:37,310
So the first one will
continue with the concept of

574
00:35:37,310 --> 00:35:41,310
pericardial effusion,
right? So as the fluid

575
00:35:41,310 --> 00:35:46,290
increases within the
pericardial space, so as you get

576
00:35:46,290 --> 00:35:48,910
more fluid there, what's
going to happen is the

577
00:35:48,910 --> 00:35:53,270
pressure is going to increase,
and that higher pericardial

578
00:35:53,270 --> 00:35:56,650
pressure is referred to
as cardiac tamponade.

579
00:35:56,890 --> 00:35:59,310
So as you get more
pressure, that's going to

580
00:35:59,310 --> 00:36:02,110
compress the heart more.
And then ultimately,

581
00:36:02,290 --> 00:36:04,770
because of that
compression, you're going to

582
00:36:04,770 --> 00:36:07,630
get a decreased cardiac
output because of it.

583
00:36:08,270 --> 00:36:11,590
Now, another complication
is constrictive

584
00:36:11,660 --> 00:36:14,590
pericarditis. And this is going

585
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:17,400
to be a result really
of inflammation.

586
00:36:17,590 --> 00:36:21,990
So chronic inflammation
that leads to fibrosis

587
00:36:21,990 --> 00:36:24,250
and calcification
of the pericardium.

588
00:36:24,250 --> 00:36:28,490
pericardium. So if the
pericardium is becoming

589
00:36:28,490 --> 00:36:31,150
more rigid, it's not
going to expand as much.

590
00:36:31,580 --> 00:36:34,850
And then obviously, you're
going to get a smaller

591
00:36:34,850 --> 00:36:39,610
blood volume and a decrease
in ventricular filling

592
00:36:39,610 --> 00:36:42,470
because of that. Now, this
is certainly going to be a

593
00:36:42,470 --> 00:36:46,330
potential complication of
tuberculosis, where you have

594
00:36:46,330 --> 00:36:50,970
mycobacterium tuberculosis
causing, being the common

595
00:36:50,970 --> 00:36:56,210
cause of subacute chronic
forms of pericarditis.

596
00:36:57,130 --> 00:37:02,080
Now, in general, in
terms of treatment, the

597
00:37:02,080 --> 00:37:04,630
treatment is really going
to depend on what the

598
00:37:04,630 --> 00:37:09,080
causative agent of that
pericarditis would be.

599
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:11,560
And so if we're talking
about a viral cause,

600
00:37:11,570 --> 00:37:15,390
then, you know, probably
just symptom management

601
00:37:15,390 --> 00:37:17,850
and some supportive
care would be enough.

602
00:37:17,870 --> 00:37:21,330
If instead you have a
bacterial or a fungal

603
00:37:21,330 --> 00:37:24,210
source, then using
antimicrobial agents

604
00:37:24,210 --> 00:37:27,830
would certainly be the
best bet, in addition

605
00:37:27,830 --> 00:37:31,730
to generalized anti
-inflammatories. So

606
00:37:46,220 --> 00:37:48,540
that concludes the
lecture. I just wanted

607
00:37:48,540 --> 00:37:50,660
to thank everyone
for listening, and I

608
00:37:50,660 --> 00:37:52,880
wanted to provide the
link for feedback.

609
00:37:53,580 --> 00:37:54,540
Thank you.